  "ingredients": [
    "16 ounce boneless, skinless chicken thighs",
    "1 tablespoon olive oil",
    "1 teaspoon cumin",
    "1/2 teaspoon chili powder",
    "1/2 teaspoon garlic powder",
    "1/2 teaspoon salt",
    "1/2 teaspoon black pepper",
    "1 tablespoon butter",
    "16 ounce broccoli (chopped)",
    "1/2 medium red onion (diced)",
    "1 1/2 medium jalapeno pepper (seeded + diced)",
    "2 teaspoon fresh garlic (minced)",
    "6 tablespoon heavy cream",
    "1/4 cup chicken broth",
    "2 ounce cream cheese",
    "1 cup cheddar cheese (shredded + divided)",
    "1/2 medium jalapeno pepper",
    "1/4 medium red onion"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Measure out and prepare all the ingredients.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/jalapeno-chicken-skillet-meal/#wprm-recipe-53789-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Jalapeno-Popper-Chicken-Meal-1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a bowl, combine the seasonings: cumin, chili powder, garlic powder, salt, and pepper. Mix until combined well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/jalapeno-chicken-skillet-meal/#wprm-recipe-53789-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Jalapeno-Popper-Chicken-Meal-2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add olive oil to a skillet on medium heat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/jalapeno-chicken-skillet-meal/#wprm-recipe-53789-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Jalapeno-Popper-Chicken-Meal-3.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the seasoning mixture onto the raw chicken.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/jalapeno-chicken-skillet-meal/#wprm-recipe-53789-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Jalapeno-Popper-Chicken-Meal-4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the chicken thighs to the skillet and cook for 2-4 minutes on each side or until internal temperature reaches 165F. Remove the chicken and set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/jalapeno-chicken-skillet-meal/#wprm-recipe-53789-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Jalapeno-Popper-Chicken-Meal-5.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add butter, broccoli, onion, jalapeno pepper, and garlic to the skillet.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/jalapeno-chicken-skillet-meal/#wprm-recipe-53789-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Jalapeno-Popper-Chicken-Meal-6.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir this together and cook for 3-4 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/jalapeno-chicken-skillet-meal/#wprm-recipe-53789-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Jalapeno-Popper-Chicken-Meal-7.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the heavy cream, chicken broth, and cream cheese to the vegetables and stir together. Lower the temperature to low.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/jalapeno-chicken-skillet-meal/#wprm-recipe-53789-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Jalapeno-Popper-Chicken-Meal-8.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir together until well combined. Add half of the shredded cheese and stir well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/jalapeno-chicken-skillet-meal/#wprm-recipe-53789-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Jalapeno-Popper-Chicken-Meal-9.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the cooked chicken to the skillet then add the rest of the shredded cheese on top.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/jalapeno-chicken-skillet-meal/#wprm-recipe-53789-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Jalapeno-Popper-Chicken-Meal-10.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Don't stir and put a lid over the skillet. Let this simmer for 7-8 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/jalapeno-chicken-skillet-meal/#wprm-recipe-53789-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Jalapeno-Popper-Chicken-Meal-11.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Garnish with jalapeno peppers and diced onions.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/jalapeno-chicken-skillet-meal/#wprm-recipe-53789-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
